## 7. Post-Run Review Structure

After completing the playbook, assess:

### What Went Well
- Phases that completed on first attempt
- Decisions that didn't require revision
- Human-AI collaboration that worked smoothly

### What Didn't Go Well
- Phases that required multiple iterations
- Decisions that were reversed
- Blockers that required escalation

### What Should Change
- Tasks that were unclear
- Gates that were too strict or too loose
- KB entries that were missing or unhelpful

### Metrics Target vs Actual

| Metric | Target | Actual | Notes |
|--------|--------|-------|-------|
| Total phases | 17 | — | |
| Tasks completed | — | — | |
| Gates passed first try | — | — | |
| Escalations | — | — | |
| Human interventions | — | — | |

### Quality Assessment

- Did the plugin meet all success criteria?
- Were all cross-cutting concerns addressed?
- Is the KB more useful after this run?

### Recommendations for Next Run

- What to add to KB
- What to change in playbook
- What to document better